For your **Distributed Web-Based Chat Application**, the prototype should demonstrate the complete user journey before development. Below is a concise prototype specification you can include in your project documentation.

# Prototype

## Prototype Overview

The prototype represents the initial visual and functional design of the Distributed Web-Based Chat Application. It illustrates the application's layout, navigation, and user interactions without implementing the complete backend logic. The objective is to validate the user experience, interface design, and workflow before full-scale development.

The prototype focuses on simplicity, usability, and responsive design while reflecting the final architecture of the application. It includes authentication, messaging, group communication, notifications, and profile management.

